WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.627 --> 00:00:04.546
Trying is about a couple who
decide to

00:00:04.546 --> 00:00:07.132
embark on parenthood and realize
that they can't.

00:00:07.132 --> 00:00:09.009
So they look into other options.

00:00:09.009 --> 00:00:10.969
I think I'm ready to talk about
adopting.

00:00:10.969 --> 00:00:11.970
Yea!

00:00:11.970 --> 00:00:13.555
Esther:
And they decide to go through
that process.

00:00:13.555 --> 00:00:16.099
Which is a lot harder than I
think they realize.

00:00:16.099 --> 00:00:17.809
Sandra:
You totally sure about this?

00:00:17.809 --> 00:00:19.311
You gotta be careful with
adoption.

00:00:19.311 --> 00:00:22.314
Mel, from the club got a rescue
dog, shat everywhere.

00:00:22.314 --> 00:00:24.483
I don't know what I'm supposed
to do with that information.

00:00:24.483 --> 00:00:25.943
♪♪

00:00:25.943 --> 00:00:29.404
I play a social worker who's
helping a couple to try and
adopt.

00:00:29.404 --> 00:00:30.864
I can get a little bit personal.

00:00:30.864 --> 00:00:32.574
-Yea, no that's fine.
-Go for it.

00:00:32.574 --> 00:00:34.076
How often would you say you
have sex?

00:00:34.952 --> 00:00:36.453
Andy:
I was adopted as a young child.

00:00:36.453 --> 00:00:39.039
You don't often hear about the
process and how difficult that
is.

00:00:39.039 --> 00:00:42.125
Andy:
And I just think it's ripe for 
a really fantastic series.

00:00:42.125 --> 00:00:43.460
I'm so excited.

00:00:43.877 --> 00:00:46.129
Part of the fun is gonna be
watching how these two people

00:00:46.129 --> 00:00:50.676
respond to being judged on
whether you are a good enough
person to adopt a child.

00:00:50.676 --> 00:00:53.136
We should make a list of the
flaws that we wanna iron out.

00:00:53.136 --> 00:00:54.137
You drink too much.

00:00:54.137 --> 00:00:56.848
You need to work on your anger.

00:00:56.848 --> 00:00:57.849
Fine put it down.

00:00:57.849 --> 00:00:59.142
♪♪

00:00:59.142 --> 00:01:01.395
The having to grow up 
and maybe realize

00:01:01.395 --> 00:01:03.939
yourself as an adult and
what that means.

00:01:03.939 --> 00:01:05.065
No!

00:01:05.065 --> 00:01:07.818
Talk to your children!

00:01:07.818 --> 00:01:09.444
They're not my children!

00:01:09.444 --> 00:01:12.072
Haha.
I don't think I'm ever going to
feel like an adult.

00:01:12.072 --> 00:01:13.407
 ♪♪

00:01:13.407 --> 00:01:15.617
We're all trying to make sense
of it... Hahaha.

00:01:15.617 --> 00:01:19.121
That's suggests an air of um,
calmness and dependability.

00:01:19.121 --> 00:01:20.747
Yeah, I like that.

00:01:20.747 --> 00:01:22.624
At the end of the day, it's 
about what's missing 

00:01:22.624 --> 00:01:25.585
and it's about what we do to
fill that hole.

00:01:25.585 --> 00:01:27.170
Crazy people don't know they're
crazy.

00:01:27.170 --> 00:01:28.213
And yet here we are.

00:01:28.213 --> 00:01:29.756
♪♪

00:01:29.756 --> 00:01:31.800
I think we are gonna to be
amazing parents.

00:01:31.800 --> 00:01:32.801
(Cork-pops)

00:01:32.801 --> 00:01:35.053
♪♪

